## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/br.png" alt="Brazil" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />Brazil

Brazil operates as a continental-scale middle power practicing strategic multi-alignment between Western institutions and Global South platforms, now with more assertive sovereignty positioning against US interventionism. Under Lula III, the country confronts persistent fiscal rigidity and deepening China dependency while the political system remains structured around Lula-Bolsonaro polarization despite the former president's imprisonment. Both sides demonstrate continued mobilization capacity heading into a highly competitive 2026 election. Institutional legitimacy faces pressure through STF internal crisis over Master Bank case handling while coalition presidentialism requires constant Centrão bargaining.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** Lula called the US capture of Maduro 'another lamentable chapter in the continuous erosion of international law,' stating this is the first time in 200+ years that South America suffered direct US military attack. Declared Brazil will not submit to hegemonic projects while maintaining dialogue with Washington. *([G1](https://g1.globo.com/economia/noticia/2026/01/18/lula-artigo-eua-venezuela-nyt.ghtml), 2026-01-18)*
- **Diplomatic:** 45-minute call where Xi emphasized protecting Global South interests and strengthening UN role. Occurred same day as Trump's Gaza Peace Council launch. Lula announced visa exemptions for Chinese citizens in reciprocity for China's 2025 measure. *([G1](https://g1.globo.com/politica/noticia/2026/01/23/lula-e-xi-conversa-telefone.ghtml), 2026-01-23)*
- **Diplomatic:** Invitation described as 'diplomatic trap' forcing choice between accepting and subordinating to US-controlled framework or declining and assuming public misalignment. Analysis notes this exposes Lula to 'difficult choice' that constrains multi-alignment strategy. *([Gazeta do Povo](https://www.gazetadopovo.com.br/republica/trump-pressiona-lula-com-armadilha-diplomatica-em-convite-para-conselho-de-paz-para-gaza/), 2026-01-19)*
- **Domestic:** In private meeting, Lula indicated plans to repeat winning ticket with VP Alckmin, saying 'in a winning team, you don't change players.' Also discussed São Paulo electoral scenarios with different roles for Haddad depending on Tarcísio's presidential intentions. *([Veja](https://veja.abril.com.br/politica/a-reuniao-em-que-lula-sinalizou-que-repetira-chapa-com-alckmin-em-2026/), 2026-01-18)*
- **Domestic:** Rally organized by Deputy Nikolas Ferreira drew ~18,000 people calling for Bolsonaro's release and other January 8 convictions. Demonstrates continued mobilization capacity despite former president's imprisonment and ineligibility. *([G1](https://g1.globo.com/df/distrito-federal/noticia/2026/01/25/manifestacao-pela-liberdade-de-bolsonaro-reune-18-mil-pessoas-em-brasilia-diz-ong.ghtml), 2026-01-25)*

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **PT strategizes 2026 elections across multiple states** — The Workers' Party is organizing electoral strategies for 2026, including pressuring Fernando Haddad to run for Senate in São Paulo, negotiating Marina Silva's potential return to the party, and defining candidates across various states including Pernambuco, Rio Grande do Norte, and Rio Grande do Sul. *([g1.globo.com](https://g1.globo.com/politica/blog/julia-duailibi/post/2026/01/22/pt-haddad-candidatura-sp.ghtml))*
- **Haddad discusses economic policy and potential 2026 candidacy** — Finance Minister Fernando Haddad addressed economic challenges, attributing public debt pressure to high interest rates rather than fiscal deficits. He discussed his potential departure from the ministry for 2026 elections and proposed transferring investment fund oversight from CVM to the Central Bank following the Master Bank scandal. *([agenciabrasil.ebc.com.br](https://g1.globo.com/economia/noticia/2026/01/19/apos-escandalo-no-banco-master-haddad-quer-banco-central-fiscalizando-e-regulando-fundos-de-investimento-hoje-na-cvm.ghtml))*
- **Arthur Lira and Hugo Motta accused of pressuring TCU in Master Bank case** — Senator Renan Calheiros accused Chamber of Deputies President Hugo Motta and former President Arthur Lira of pressuring the Federal Court of Accounts (TCU) regarding the Master Bank case. Lira denied the accusations, calling them 'fake news' aimed at gaining media attention. *([jc.uol.com.br](https://www.estadao.com.br/politica/calheiros-diz-que-motta-e-lira-pressionaram-tcu-para-anular-liquidacao-do-master/))*
- **Polls show Lula leading 2026 presidential scenarios against Bolsonaro family** — New polling by Apex/Futura shows President Lula leading in most first-round scenarios for the 2026 presidential election, though Senator Flávio Bolsonaro leads in some configurations and wins in simulated second-round matchups. The polls tested various scenarios including potential candidates like Governor Tarcísio. *([noticias.uol.com.br](https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/agencia-estado/2026/01/22/lula-e-flavio-bolsonaro-lideram-em-cenario-com-tarcisio-no-1-turno-aponta-pesquisa.htm))*
- **PT uses AI-generated content to counter Pix disinformation campaign** — PT-linked communication networks launched AI-generated videos to counter false information about Pix payment system taxation, including content that portrayed opponents as 'cockroaches.' The campaign responded to disinformation spread by right-wing figures about government tax policies. *([infomoney.com.br](https://infomoney.com.br/politica/rede-do-pt-usa-ia-brava-para-desmentir-fake-do-pix-e-associa-direita-a-baratas))*
- **ABIN requests authorization for new civil service examination** — The Brazilian Intelligence Agency (ABIN) submitted a request to the Ministry of Management and Innovation for authorization to hold a new public examination to fill positions across four career tracks, with salaries up to R$19,000. The request remains under analysis. *([apostilasopcao.com.br](https://www.apostilasopcao.com.br/blog/abin/))*
</Accordion>


